<Article
  title="What comes in a brake pad set? | Parts Relay"
  description="Find out how to ask which pads, wear sensors and fitting hardware a brake quote includes."
  heading="What comes in a brake pad set?"
  topic="Repair shops"
  topicHref="/journal/"
  readTime="3 min read"
  relatedHeading="More parts-counter notes"
  related={related}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    “Pads” on the repair order makes sense to the technician who inspected the brakes. At the parts
    counter it leaves two questions open. Which axle? And what else does the shop expect in the box?
  </Fragment>
  <div
    slot="cover"
    class="lib-art lib-art-pads"
    aria-label="Illustration of a brake disc and separated pad set"
    role="img"
  >
    <span>Front axle</span>
    <img src="/assets/brake-pads.svg" alt="" />
    <b>PAD SET</b>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Put the axle on the enquiry</h2>
    <p>
      If the front brakes are due, write “front brake pad set.” The distributor can check the
      reference for that axle on the vehicle. If the technician has called for a new wear sensor,
      put that on the enquiry too.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Ask about the set on the quote</h2>
    <p>
      Try asking, “Does the front set include the wear sensor this job needs?” Clips and shims are
      worth checking too if the technician has called for them. A supplier can tell you what comes
      with the particular set they’re quoting.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="lib-case">
    <h2>Reading the supplier’s answer</h2>
    <p>
      When a supplier quotes a set with clips and lists the sensor separately, the repair order
      needs to account for both references.
    </p>
    <dl class="lib-evidence">
      <div>
        <dt>Front pad set</dt>
        <dd>
          Write down the quoted reference. Check it against the vehicle and axle on the repair
          order.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Clips</dt>
        <dd>Mark these as included so the shop doesn’t ask for a second set.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Wear sensor</dt>
        <dd>
          Get its own reference and the quantity required. Check availability for both the pads and
          the sensor before booking the job.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <p>
    <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/tools/part-details/">
      How to read a quoted part number
      <svg
        aria-hidden="true"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
